# Binaries for programs and plugins
*.exe
*.exe~
*.dll
*.so
*.dylib

# Local configuration files
doc/config*
doc/deploy*

# The real config, wherever the loader looks for it.
#
# internal/config/load.go:180 adds "." to the search path and keys.go:6 names the file
# "apiserver", so a config placed in the REPO ROOT is loaded automatically -- and
# doc/postgres-cutover.md:38 documents exactly that filename carrying a live Postgres DSN.
# Without these lines the natural setup (copy the example, fill in the real password,
# `git add -A`) commits production credentials. The ignores above only covered doc/.
/apiserver.json
/apiserver.yaml
/apiserver.yml
/apiserver.toml
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Test binary, built with `go test -c`
*.test

# Output of the go coverage tool, specifically when used with LiteIDE
*.out

# Dependency directories (remove the comment below to include it)
vendor/

# Idea IDE
.idea/

# MacOS
**/.DS_Store
